Q('B2-L123','Exam Lab 13 (TOEFL · IELTS · college)',
 'eu consigo treinar as perguntas de informação factual e de informação negativa (NOT) em uma notícia, como no TOEFL Reading.',
 ('Reading · A news report',news('Report: Council Approves Bike-Lane Budget',['The city council **approved** a bike-lane budget on Tuesday by a vote of 7 to 4. The plan **includes** protected lanes on Main Street, new signals and a repair fund, but it **does not include** a bike-share scheme.','Councillor Rui Matos said the vote was “long overdue.” Opponents **argued** that parking would be **lost**, while supporters **pointed out** that traffic deaths **have fallen** where lanes were built.'],kicker='CITY NEWS',by='By Elisa Prado',gloss=[('budget','orçamento'),('overdue','atrasado'),('signal','sinal'),('scheme','programa')])),
 [('The budget was approved 7 to 4.','T','7 to 4.'),('The plan includes a bike-share scheme.','F','does not include.'),('Supporters say traffic deaths have fallen where lanes were built.','T','have fallen.')],
 [('“overdue” = ?',['atrasado há muito','devido','dívida'],0,'overdue.'),('“scheme” = ?',['programa','esquema só','escola'],0,'scheme.')],
 G('Perguntas factual e NOT no TOEFL Reading',['Tipo','Estratégia'],[['Factual','achar a frase exata no texto'],['NOT / EXCEPT','eliminar o que o texto menciona'],['Inference','concluir sem copiar'],['Rhetorical purpose','função do trecho']],'Em perguntas **NOT**, três opções estão no texto e **uma não**. Risque as que você acha no texto e escolha a que sobra.'),
 [('The council ___ the budget on Tuesday. (approve, past)','approved','passado.',None),('The plan does not ___ a bike-share scheme. (include)','include','negativa.',None),('Opponents ___ that parking would be lost. (argue, past)','argued','verbo de relato.',None),('Traffic deaths have ___ where lanes were built. (fall, part.)','fallen','particípio.',None)],
 V('bike-lane budget=orçamento para ciclovias|protected lane=faixa protegida|councillor=vereador|seven-to-four vote=votação de sete a quatro|repair fund=fundo de reparos|parking loss=perda de vagas|traffic fatality=morte no trânsito|lane signal=semáforo de ciclovia|pedestrian refuge=refúgio para pedestres|capital plan=plano de investimento|motion carried=moção aprovada|dissenting vote=voto divergente|cycling advocate=defensor do ciclismo|street redesign=redesenho de rua|speed hump=lombada|kerb extension=extensão de calçada|commuter route=rota de quem vai ao trabalho|bus priority=prioridade para ônibus|road diet=redução de faixas|contractor bid=proposta de empreiteira|minutes of meeting=ata da reunião|public gallery=galeria pública|fact question=pergunta factual|negative fact=informação negativa|elimination method=método de eliminação|line reference=referência de linha|highlighted sentence=frase destacada|city budget=orçamento da cidade'),
 ('Study',[('Student','Does the plan include a bike-share scheme?','O plano inclui um programa de bicicletas compartilhadas?'),('Tutor','No. That is the “NOT” answer.','Não. Essa é a resposta “NOT”.'),('Student','How do I find it fast?','Como acho rápido?'),('Tutor','Cross out what the text mentions.','Risque o que o texto menciona.')]),
 [('Report a fact.','Relate.','The council approved the budget.'),('Say what is not included.','Diga.','It does not include a bike-share scheme.'),('Report a reason.','Relate.','Supporters pointed out that deaths have fallen.')],
 ('Summarize the news in 4 sentences using approve, include and argue.','The council approved a bike-lane budget by seven votes to four. The plan includes protected lanes and a repair fund. It does not include a bike-share scheme. Opponents argued that parking would be lost.',['Usei **approve**','Usei **include**','Usei **argue**'],'4 frases'),
 exam=['TOEFL Reading, pergunta NOT/EXCEPT: três opções aparecem no texto; escolha a ausente.','Perguntas factuais: localize a palavra-chave e leia a frase inteira.','Marque a linha no texto para não reler tudo.'],
 verbs=[('approve','aprovar','Councils approve budgets.','Conselhos aprovam orçamentos.')],expr=[('Long overdue.','Há muito atrasado.'),('By a narrow margin.','Por pouco.'),('Back the plan.','Apoiar o plano.'),('Put it on the table.','Colocar em pauta.'),('Foot the bill.','Arcar com a conta.'),('Break new ground.','Abrir novos caminhos.')])
Q('B2-L124','Integrated communication: Politics as a topic of discussion',
 'eu consigo integrar leitura, escuta, fala e escrita sobre política numa biografia de uma jovem ativista fictícia.',
 ('Reading · A biography',bio('Marina Duarte (fictional)',['Marina Duarte **was elected** to her city council at 24. Before that, she **had her campaign posters printed** in a school lab and **got her first speech written** by a friend. She **is expected to** run for mayor, and she **must have worked** harder than anyone.','Critics say she **might have been** helped by luck, but friends say she **can’t have** won without the door-to-door work.'],years='Born 1998',facts=[('Job','vereadora'),('Country','Brasil'),('Famous for','campanha de rua')],gloss=[('poster','cartaz'),('mayor','prefeito'),('campaign','campanha'),('luck','sorte')])),
 [('Marina was elected at 24.','T','at 24.'),('She wrote every speech herself.','F','got her first speech written.'),('Friends say her door-to-door work mattered.','T','door-to-door.')],
 [('“poster” = ?',['cartaz','poste','postal'],0,'poster.'),('“luck” = ?',['sorte','luz','lucro'],0,'luck.')],
 G('Revisão: passiva, have something done, dedução',['Estrutura','Exemplo'],[['passiva','She **was elected**.'],['have + obj + part.','She **had** posters **printed**.'],['be expected to','She **is expected to** run.'],['must / can’t have','She **must have worked** hard.']],'Combine **passiva**, **causativa** e **dedução** no mesmo perfil.'),
 [('She ___ elected at 24. (be, past)','was','passiva.',None),('She had her posters ___ . (print, part.)','printed','have + part.',None),('She is ___ to run for mayor. (expected)','expected','be expected to.',None),('She must have ___ hard. (work, part.)','worked','must have.',None)],
 V('first-term councillor=vereadora de primeiro mandato|ward election=eleição distrital|door-knocking=batida de porta em porta|campaign poster=cartaz de campanha|campaign slogan=slogan de campanha|youth candidate=candidata jovem|swearing-in=cerimônia de posse|constituency office=escritório de distrito|volunteer canvasser=cabo eleitoral voluntário|leaflet run=rodada de folhetos|rally speech=discurso de comício|bake-sale fundraiser=venda de bolos para arrecadar fundos|poll lead=liderança nas pesquisas|ballot count=contagem de votos|victory speech=discurso de vitória|school lab=laboratório da escola|print shop=gráfica|first speech=primeiro discurso|political newcomer=novata na política|ward meeting=reunião de bairro|local paper=jornal local|council chamber=plenário municipal|policy platform=plataforma de políticas|grassroots effort=esforço de base|swing ward=distrito indeciso|campaign manager=coordenador de campanha|mayoral bid=candidatura à prefeitura'),
 ('Interview prep',[('Ana','How did Marina win?','Como a Marina ganhou?'),('Leo','She had her posters printed at school.','Ela mandou imprimir os cartazes na escola.'),('Ana','Is she expected to run for mayor?','Espera-se que ela se candidate a prefeita?'),('Leo','Yes. She must have worked very hard.','Sim. Ela deve ter trabalhado muito.')]),
 [('Use have + object + participle.','Use.','She had her posters printed.'),('Use must have.','Use.','She must have worked hard.'),('Use be expected to.','Use.','She is expected to run.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence biography of a local leader, real or fictional.','Marina was elected at 24. She had her posters printed at school. A friend wrote her first speech. She is expected to run for mayor. She must have worked harder than anyone. Critics say luck helped, but friends disagree.',['Usei **passiva**','Usei **have something done**','Usei **must have**'],'6 frases'),
 verbs=[('elect','eleger','People elect leaders.','As pessoas elegem líderes.')],expr=[('Run for office.','Candidatar-se a um cargo.'),('Grassroots support.','Apoio de base.'),('Win by a landslide.','Vencer com folga.'),('Step up.','Dar um passo à frente.'),('Hit the ground running.','Começar a todo vapor.'),('Fresh blood.','Sangue novo.')])
Q('B2-L125','Advanced Passive Voice — practice and contrast',
 'eu consigo contrastar voz ativa e passiva avançada num poema e usar lead e miss out on.',
 ('Reading · A poem',poem('Who Is Led?',['The crowd is led, the crowd is told,','the flag is raised, the speech is sold;','but those who stay at home are missed—','don’t miss out on the voting list!','Laws are made and laws are changed,','by tired hands and hearts arranged;','may all be heard, may none be lost,','whatever it may cost.'],by='Original poem for advanced learners',gloss=[('crowd','multidão'),('flag','bandeira'),('hand','mão'),('cost','custo')])),
 [('The poem says people at home are missed.','T','are missed.'),('The poem says laws never change.','F','laws are changed.'),('The poet wants everyone to be heard.','T','may all be heard.')],
 [('“crowd” = ?',['multidão','coroa','criança'],0,'crowd.'),('“flag” = ?',['bandeira','flauta','chama'],0,'flag.')],
 G('Ativa × passiva avançada',['Ativa','Passiva'],[['Leaders lead the crowd.','The crowd **is led**.'],['Someone has changed the law.','The law **has been changed**.'],['They are making laws.','Laws **are being made**.'],['They must hear everyone.','Everyone **must be heard**.']],'Use a **passiva** quando o agente é **desconhecido, óbvio ou irrelevante**. Use **by + agente** só se for importante.'),
 [('The crowd is ___ . (lead, part.)','led','passiva.',None),('Laws are ___ made right now. (being)','being','contínuo passivo.',None),('Everyone must be ___ . (hear, part.)','heard','modal passivo.',None),('Don’t ___ out on the voting list! (miss)','miss','miss out on.',None)],
 V('voting list=lista de votação|crowd noise=barulho da multidão|raised flag=bandeira hasteada|speech platform=palanque de discurso|tired hands=mãos cansadas|heartfelt plea=apelo sincero|stay-at-home voter=eleitor que não sai de casa|ignored voice=voz ignorada|silent majority=maioria silenciosa|rousing chant=canto inflamado|banner wave=ondular de faixas|placard=cartaz de protesto|megaphone=megafone|street march=marcha de rua|public square=praça pública|echoing hall=salão com eco|marching band=banda marcial|campaign anthem=hino de campanha|rhyming couplet=dístico rimado|poetic refrain=refrão poético|stanza break=quebra de estrofe|verse rhythm=ritmo do verso|metaphor of voice=metáfora da voz|rally crowd=multidão de comício|ballot dream=sonho de voto|hopeful verse=verso esperançoso|fading cheer=aplauso que se apaga|rousing speech=discurso inflamado'),
 ('Poetry circle',[('Ana','Who is led in the poem?','Quem é conduzido no poema?'),('Leo','The crowd is led and told what to do.','A multidão é conduzida e recebe ordens.'),('Ana','What shouldn’t we miss out on?','O que não devemos perder?'),('Leo','The chance to vote.','A chance de votar.')]),
 [('Change active to passive.','Mude.','The crowd is led by the speaker.'),('Use miss out on.','Use.','Don’t miss out on the vote.'),('Use lead.','Use.','Who will lead the march?')],
 ('Write 5 sentences, each in the passive, about an election.','Votes are counted at night. The result has been announced. Posters are being removed from the streets. Every voice must be heard. The winner will be congratulated by all.',['Usei **passiva**','5 frases'],'5 frases'),
 verbs=[('lead','liderar; conduzir','She leads the march.','Ela lidera a marcha.')],pv=[('miss out on','perder (oportunidade)','Don’t miss out on this chance.','Não perca esta chance.')],expr=[('Lead by example.','Liderar pelo exemplo.'),('Rally around.','Unir-se em torno de.'),('Raise the flag.','Hastear a bandeira.'),('Speak up.','Falar em voz alta.'),('Have a voice.','Ter voz.'),('Count me in.','Pode contar comigo.')])
Q('B2-L126','Deduction about the past (must have, can’t have) — form',
 'eu consigo formar deduções sobre o passado com must have e can’t have numa charge sobre uma eleição.',
 ('Reading · A comic strip',comic('Who Took the Banner?',[dict(scene='🪧',bubbles=[('Ana','The banner is gone!'),('Leo','Someone must have taken it.')],cap='Panel 1'),dict(scene='🔍',bubbles=[('Ana','It can’t have been the guard. He was asleep.'),('Leo','Then it must have been the wind.')],cap='Panel 2'),dict(scene='🎈',bubbles=[('Leo','Look! It’s on the roof!'),('Ana','It must have flown up there.')],cap='Panel 3')],gloss=[('banner','faixa'),('guard','guarda'),('roof','telhado'),('wind','vento')])),
 [('Leo thinks someone took the banner.','T','must have taken it.'),('Ana thinks the guard did it.','F','can’t have been the guard.'),('The banner was on the roof.','T','on the roof.')],
 [('“banner” = ?',['faixa','banheiro','banco'],0,'banner.'),('“roof” = ?',['telhado','raiz','rua'],0,'roof.')],
 G('must have / can’t have + particípio',['Forma','Sentido'],[['must have + part.','certeza afirmativa sobre o passado'],['can’t have + part.','certeza negativa sobre o passado'],['couldn’t have + part.','mesmo sentido, mais formal'],['Exemplo','It **must have flown** up. It **can’t have been** the guard.']],'**must have** = tenho quase certeza que **aconteceu**. **can’t have** = tenho quase certeza que **não aconteceu**. Não use **mustn’t have**.'),
 [('Someone ___ have taken it. (must)','must','must have.',None),('It ___ have been the guard. (can’t)','can’t','can’t have.',None),('It must have ___ up there. (fly, part.)','flown','particípio.',None),('He was asleep, so it couldn’t have ___ him. (be, part.)','been','particípio.',None)],
 V('election banner=faixa eleitoral|stolen sign=placa roubada|night guard=vigia noturno|gusty wind=vento forte|rooftop ledge=beiral do telhado|tangled rope=corda emaranhada|vandalism case=caso de vandalismo|security camera=câmera de segurança|campaign headquarters=sede da campanha|missing banner=faixa desaparecida|detective guess=palpite de detetive|comic panel=quadro de quadrinhos|speech bubble=balão de fala|caption box=caixa de legenda|sight gag=piada visual|cartoon villain=vilão de desenho|punchline=desfecho da piada|satire strip=tirinha de sátira|political cartoon=charge política|editorial cartoonist=chargista|inked outline=contorno a nanquim|sleepy guard=guarda sonolento|windy night=noite ventosa|banner pole=mastro da faixa|clue board=quadro de pistas|puzzled look=olhar intrigado|chase scene=cena de perseguição|funny mix-up=confusão engraçada'),
 ('Comic club',[('Ana','Who took the banner?','Quem pegou a faixa?'),('Leo','It can’t have been the guard. He was asleep.','Não pode ter sido o guarda. Ele dormia.'),('Ana','Then the wind must have taken it.','Então o vento deve tê-la levado.'),('Leo','Yes, it must have flown to the roof.','Sim, deve ter voado para o telhado.')]),
 [('Make a strong guess.','Faça uma dedução.','She must have forgotten.'),('Say it was impossible.','Diga.','He can’t have known.'),('Explain your guess.','Explique.','The lights are on, so he must have come back.')],
 ('Write 5 sentences using must have and can’t have about a mystery.','The window is open, so someone must have come in. It can’t have been the cat. The floor is wet, so it must have rained. My brother can’t have left, because his coat is here. He must have gone out in a hurry.',['Usei **must have**','Usei **can’t have**','5 frases'],'5 frases'),
 verbs=[('deduce','deduzir','Detectives deduce who did it.','Detetives deduzem quem foi.')],expr=[('Jump to conclusions.','Tirar conclusões precipitadas.'),('Put two and two together.','Somar os fatos.'),('Piece it together.','Montar o quebra-cabeça.'),('There’s more than meets the eye.','Há mais do que se vê.'),('Add up.','Fazer sentido.'),('A dead giveaway.','Uma pista óbvia.')])
